I don't know what the original writer thought, and I don't remember what he
wrote, but I hate keeping hitting the space bar all the time when something
attacks me. I don't suggest removing the messages, I just suggest that
the messages could use more than just the top row of the display. The
messages could be displayed after each other, on as many lines as it takes,
and the --more-- prompt could appear after the last one, or when the display
gets full.

Instead of

the nymph pretends to be friendly --More-- 
the nymph removes your blessed +9 blue dragon scale mail --More--
the nymph removes your blessed +6 blue and white shield --More--
the nymph removes your +8 hard hat --More-- 
the nymph removes your +6 hard shoes --More-- 

there might be

the nymph pretends to be friendly
the nymph removes your blessed +9 blue dragon scale mail
the nymph removes your blessed +6 blue and white shield 
the nymph removes your +8 hard hat 
the nymph removes your +6 hard shoes --More--

so that the lines would all be in the display together, and the --More--
would be prompted only when it is the player's turn to do something.
I don't know the nethack sources and I don't know how hard this would be
to do, but I don't suppose it would be impossible.
Anyway, I would consider it a great improvement on the user interface.
